{% from "components/link.jinja" import link %}
{% from "components/list.jinja" import list_item %}
{% from "components/heading.jinja" import heading %}
{% from "components/alert.jinja" import alert %}
{% macro historic_documents_content() %}
  <p>
    You can read more about how to find older records in {{ link(content="Civil court cases: Chancery Division since 1875", href="https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/help-with-your-research/research-guides/civil-court-cases-chancery-division-since-1875/", attrs={"target":"_blank"}) }}
  </p>
{% endmacro %}
{% macro court_noun_content() %}
  court
{% endmacro %}
{% macro contents_navigation() %}
  {% call list_item() %}
    {{ link(href="#coverage-on-find-case-law", content="Coverage on Find Case Law") }}
  {% endcall %}
  {% call list_item() %}
    {{ link(href="#recent-judgments", content="Recent judgments") }}
  {% endcall %}
  {% call list_item() %}
    {{ link(href="#search-this-court", content="Search this court") }}
  {% endcall %}
  {% call list_item() %}
    {{ link(href="#understanding-judgments", content="Understanding " ~ court.name ~ " judgments") }}
  {% endcall %}
  {% call list_item() %}
    {{ link(href="#about", content="About " ~ court.name) }}
  {% endcall %}
  {% call list_item() %}
    {{ link(href="#questions-about-judgments-from-this-court", content="Questions about judgments from this court") }}
  {% endcall %}
{% endmacro %}
{% macro coverage_content() %}
  {{ heading(content="Coverage on Find Case Law", tag="h2") }}
  {% set court_date_range = param|get_court_date_range %}
  {% set court_start_year = param|get_court_start_year %}
  {% set court_documents_count = court|get_court_judgments_count|intcomma %}
  <p>
    <strong>Date range</strong> — {{ court_date_range }}
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What’s included</strong> — We currently hold {{ court_documents_count }} documents from {{ court_date_range }}.
  </p>
  <p><strong>Transfer method</strong> — This court began regularly transferring judgments to The National Archives in 2022. The oldest judgment from this court included in Find Case Law is from {{ court_start_year }}. Judgments from {{ court_start_year }}–2022 were sourced from other collections.</p>
  {{ historic_documents_content() }}
{% endmacro %}
{% macro understanding_content() %}
{% endmacro %}
{% macro description_content(start_year=None) %}
  {% call alert() %}
    <p><strong>Changes to the Chancery Division</strong></p>
    <p>The Chancery Division was replaced by the {{ link(href=url("court_or_tribunal", "ewhc/bp"), content="Business and Property Division") }} on 1 October 2026.</p>
    <p>You can still find existing Chancery judgments on this service. For judgments published from 1 October 2026 onwards, check the {{ link(href=url("court_or_tribunal", "ewhc/bp"), content="Business and Property Division") }}.</p>
    <p>The Chancery Division is becoming part of the new {{ link(href=url("court_or_tribunal", "ewhc/bp"), content="Business and Property Division") }}. You can still find all existing Chancery judgments and decisions on this service. Material published from October 2026 onwards may appear under the {{ link(href=url("court_or_tribunal", "ewhc/bp"), content="Business and Property Division") }}.</p>
    <p>{{ link(href="https://www.judiciary.uk/the-lady-chief-justice-and-lord-chancellor-modernise-the-high-court-through-establishment-of-the-business-and-property-division/", content="Read more about the change on the Judiciary website") }}</p>
  {% endcall %}
  <p>The Chancery Division was a division of the High Court. It handled a wide range of civil cases including business disputes, intellectual property and probate issues.</p>
  <p>On 1 October 2026 it was replaced by the Business and Property Division.</p>
  <p>The lists that were previously under the Chancery Division now fall under the Business and Property Division. These include the Business List, Insolvency and Companies List, Property, Trusts and Probate List, and Intellectual Property List (as well as its sub-lists, the Intellectual Property Enterprise Court and Patents Court).</p>
  <p>You can read more about the decision to replace the Chancery Division on the Judiciary’s website.</p>
  <p>This court began to regularly transfer judgments to The National Archives in 2022. The oldest judgment from this court included in Find Case Law is from 2003.</p>
{% endmacro %}
{% macro about_content() %}
{% endmacro %}
